    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d418">

                <pb facs="0483" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.796/1–946: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-01-09T18:00:00-03:00">January 9, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 10—4:26 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. ReDeptel 28, January 7, 7 p.m.<anchor n="69" xml:id="d418-f1"/> Embassy has
                    made urgent and strong representations to high and influential officials,
                    including Foreign Office and Air Ministry, against Air Minister’s<anchor n="70"
                        xml:id="d418-f2"/> order revoking authority for additional flights by
                    Pan-American Airways over Barreiras cut-off. I am informed by excellent source
                    that General Dutra<anchor n="71" xml:id="d418-f3"/> is sympathetic to our point
                    of view, and likewise understand that predominant sentiment in Air Ministry,
                    military as well as civilian, supports our view. Accordingly expect favorable
                    action to be taken in cancelling latest order and am continuing to press for
                    urgent action to facilitate planning of flights and schedules.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d418-f1" n="69" xml:id="d418-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d418-f2" n="70" xml:id="d418-f2-content">
                <p>Brig. Armando Trompowski.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d418-f3" n="71" xml:id="d418-f3-content">
                <p>Gen. Enrico Gaspar Dutra, President-elect of Brazil.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
